'''''Malva olbia''''' (previously known as ''Lavatera olbia''), the '''garden tree mallow''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Malvaceae]].<ref name="RHS_507380" >{{cite web |title=''Malva olbia'' garden tree mallow |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/507380/malva-olbia/details |date=2023 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=9 February 2023 |quote=Other common names; tree lavatera ... 3 suppliers |archive-date=9 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230209125219/https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/507380/malva-olbia/details |url-status=live }}</ref> It is native to the western Mediterranean, and has been introduced to California.<ref name="POWO_561809-1" >{{cite POWO |id=561809-1 |title=''Malva olbia'' (L.) Alef. |access-date=9 February 2023 }}</ref> A vigorous perennial shrub reaching {{cvt|2.5|m|ft|0}}, the [[Royal Horticultural Society]] considers it to be a good plant to attract pollinators.<ref name="RHS_507380" /> 

==Cultivars==

It has a number of commercially available cultivars, which may be hybrids with ''[[Malva thuringiaca]]'', dubbed ''[[Malva × clementii]]''.<ref name="POWO_77100857-1" >{{cite POWO |id=77100857-1 |title=''Malva'' × ''clementii'' (Cheek) Stace |access-date=9 February 2023 }}</ref> The cultivars 'Rosea' and 'Red{{nbsp}}Rum' have gained the Royal Horticultural Society's [[Award of Garden Merit]].<ref name="RHS_224063" >{{cite web |title=''Lavatera olbia'' 'Rosea' tree mallow 'Rosea' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/224063/lavatera-olbia-rosea/details |date=2023 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=9 February 2023 |quote=Synonyms; ''Lavatera olbia'' 'Rosea', ''Lavatera thuringiaca'' 'Rosea', ''Lavatera arborea'' 'Rosea', ''Lavatera'' × ''clementii'' 'Rosea', ''Lavatera'' 'Rosea' ... 18 suppliers |archive-date=9 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230209125218/https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/224063/lavatera-olbia-rosea/details |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="RHS_226505" >{{cite web |title=''Lavatera olbia'' 'Red Rum' |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/226505/lavatera-olbia-red-rum/details |date=2023 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=9 February 2023 |quote=Synonyms; ''Malva'' × ''clementii'' 'Rigrum'<sup>PBR</sup>, ''Lavatera olbia'' 'Red Rum', ''Lavatera'' × ''clementii'' 'Rigrum', ''Lavatera thuringiaca'' 'Red Rum', ''Lavatera thuringiaca'' 'Rigrum', ''Lavatera'' × ''clementii'' 'Red Rum', ''Lavatera thuringiaca'' 'Red Rum, ''Lavatera'' × ''clementii'' Red Rum ... 14 suppliers |archive-date=9 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230209125220/https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/226505/lavatera-olbia-red-rum/details |url-status=live }}</ref> Other cultivars include 'Barnsley' (with white aging to shell pink flowers), 'Lilac Lady', 'Eye Catcher', 'Pink Frills', 'Wembdon Variegated', and 'Saxtead'.<ref name="RHS_124547" >{{cite web |title=''Lavatera olbia'' 'Barnsley' tree mallow 'Barnsley' |url=